        "message": "Here are three practical ways to handle this: 1. **Let both feelings exist without judging yourself.** You can be genuinely happy for a friend and still feel a sharp sting of envy at the exact same time. Feeling jealous doesn’t make you a bad friend; it just means this was something that mattered to you, too.\n2. **Treat the jealousy as information about what you want.** Envy usually points directly at a personal goal. Instead of focusing on why they got it, use that energy to pinpoint your own target—whether that means finding other scholarships, grants, or academic opportunities you can apply for.\n3. **Decide how to show up right now.** A brief, sincere congratulations (\"So happy for you, congratulations!\") is enough for now. You don't have to pretend to be overjoyed for hours or listen to all the details today if you need a little breathing room first.",
